MULTITX_DEMO_VAULT_XLM=CATSMPDW4JOQOCFPKD7G3JLOADELJMFUIY3CPTYL75LMXBFG7S6VE2AA
MULTITX_BLEND_CHILD=CBPKFT2AC5C4DWBE2DXPZI3C76UTDOMUTWDUTKCME5KW3IPZDBW3QNKH
MULTITX_SOROSWAP_LP_CHILD=CAWL7IHKEL73UYSLTFYXTMZB5FMJ3V3FWW57BDBCYPANJNUKABHYRTQW
# Proven on testnet (each tx within Soroban per-tx memory):
#   - single-tx deposit 100 XLM -> 30/40/30 incl. real Soroswap LP (70,068,508 LP tokens)
#   - INSTANT redeem from native buffer: one light tx, ZERO Blend/Soroswap calls
#   - QUEUED redeem > buffer (the flow that previously OOM'd): request_redeem (escrow)
#       -> drain_child(blend) [Blend pool.submit, isolated tx]
#       -> drain_child(soro)  [Soroswap remove_liquidity+swap, isolated tx]
#       -> claim_redeem [light, paid 89.88 XLM from buffer, ZERO heavy calls]  >>> SUCCEEDS
#   - rebalance_step(blend)+rebalance_step(soro) restored a drifted basket to exactly 30/30/40
# Canonical VAULT_XLM (CCY337...) left untouched on plain Blend (CAGIMEB3...).
# Demo vault retains admin's test funds (recoverable via request_redeem->drain->claim).
